d if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-29 14:23] Diana**: If we defer, we should at least write down the v1.1 requirements so we don't lose them.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:01] Alice**: Team, we're falling behind on core engine work. I'm deferring the auth module to v1.1. For v1.0, the API assumes a trusted local network.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:19] Diana**: Manageable if we stay local-network-only. I'll note the deferral.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:21] Bob**: Fine. I'll keep the seams clean so adding auth later isn't a rewrite.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:04] Bob**: Still deferred — capturing v1.1 auth requirements while we remember them: REST auth with rotation support, since v1.0 is local-network-only.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:06] Diana**: Agreed. Folding that into the deferred-work notes so it survives until v1.1 planning.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 10:11] Alice**: Rechecked release scope for v1.0 — auth stays deferred to post-v1.0.0. Trusted-network assumption still holds.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 08 slack thread api authent deferr channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 06 28 13 07 bob look into rest api auth for v1 0 do we need a full auth stori now or is trust local network enough for the first releas 2026 06 28 13 22 diana given the pii involv someth robust would be nice but if this is strict local network onli we might not need it for v1 0 2026 06 28 14 00 bob do a short studi either way what we d need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer 2026 06 29 14 23 diana if we defer we should at least write down the v1 1 requir so we don t lose them 2026 06 30 09 01 alic team we re fall behind on core engin work i m defer the auth modul to v1 1 for v1 0 the api assum a trust local network 2026 06 30 09 19 diana manag if we stay local network onli i ll note the deferr 2026 06 30 09 21 bob fine i ll keep the seam clean so ad auth later isn t a rewrit 2026 08 0511 04 bob still defer captur v1 1 auth requir while we 